---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ELSEWHERE } from '../consts';

// One contact route rather than a second copy of the footer's link list.
const linkedin = ELSEWHERE.find((link) => link.label === 'LinkedIn');
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ryan Nel — Senior Staff Software Engineer in Gothenburg, working on large software systems and AI engineering."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <div class="prose page-prose">
    <p>
      I’m Ryan Nel, a Senior Staff Software Engineer in Gothenburg. I work on large-scale software
      systems, and increasingly on the systems we build <em>with</em> AI rather than around it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of what interests me sits at the boundary between the two: how you give a system enough
      of the right context to reason well, where agents stop understanding a codebase, how to
      evaluate any of it honestly, and what architecture looks like when a component can be
      confidently wrong.
    </p>
    <p>
      I learn by building. The notes here are the residue of that — what I tried, what surprised me,
      what didn’t work, and what I currently think. I’d rather write something specific and
      provisional than something general and confident.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing here reflects or discloses my employer’s work. Where a lesson comes from professional
      experience, it’s generalised.
    </p>
    <p>
      If any of it is useful, or wrong, I’d like to hear about it —
      {linkedin ? <a href={linkedin.href} rel="me">LinkedIn</a> : 'get in touch'} is the surest way
      to reach me.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
